<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net461;netcoreapp2.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <RuntimeIdentifiers>win-x64</RuntimeIdentifiers>
    <Platforms>x64</Platforms>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <RootNamespace>Lennox.NvEncSharp</RootNamespace>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <Version>2.2.0</Version>
    <!-- CI can package the checked-in native DLL without installing CUDA or Visual C++. -->
    <BuildCudaLibrary Condition="'$(BuildCudaLibrary)' == ''">true</BuildCudaLibrary>

    <PackageId>Lennox.NvEncSharp</PackageId>
    <PackageReadmeFile>readme.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageReleaseNotes><![CDATA[NvEncSharp 2.2.0 fixes encoding, decoding, color conversion, and native interop issues. (BREAKING CHANGE)

Breaking changes
- Removed NvEncRegisterResourceEx.AsInputPointer() and .AsOutputPointer(). Registered resource handles must be mapped with NvEncoder.MapInputResource() before encoding. Use the returned MappedResource and MappedBufferFmt, then unmap before unregistering. For bitstream output, use NvEncoder.CreateBitstreamBuffer().
- Changed LibCuVideo.GetDecodeStatus()'s output parameter to CuVideoGetDecodeStatus, matching the native API and fixing a potential memory corruption issue. The CuVideoDecoder.GetDecodeStatus() wrapper still returns CuVideoDecodeStatus.

Library fixes
- Fixed generated bitfield accessors, including masks, offsets, and signed values, and regenerated the affected structures.
- Fixed CuVideoFormat.VideoFormat and VideoFullRange bit accessors.
- Corrected NV_ENC_CREATE_INPUT_BUFFER_VER for input buffer creation.
- Fixed missing structure versions in GetEncodePresetConfig(). Marked its overloads obsolete; use GetEncodePresetConfigEx() for P1-P7 presets.
- Fixed NAL packet parsing when data precedes a start code.
- Fixed CUDA color conversion that truncated pixel values, including incorrect RGB24 packing. Updated the bundled native DLL.

Sample fixes
- Fixed screen capture encoding to use mapped resources and release them in the correct order.
- Restored decoded frame copies to host memory.
- Fixed video playback timing and frame queuing, with a 30 FPS fallback when timing metadata is unavailable.
- Fixed buffered NAL submission and end-of-stream flushing.
- Added explicit rejection of unsupported video formats in the decoding sample, which supports 8-bit 4:2:0 H.264 with NV12 output.
- Improved decoding sample shutdown and resource cleanup.

Added Windows x64 native structure size and field offset validation, and expanded NAL parsing tests.]]></PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Title>NvEncSharp</Title>
    <PackageDescription>NvEncSharp provides a dotnet core and .net framework interface to Nvidia's NvEnc hardware video encoder (nvEncodeAPI), the CUDA video decoder (nvcuvid), and the CUDA APIs (nvcuda). This package requires 64bit targets.</PackageDescription>
    <Authors>Joseph Lennox</Authors>
    <Copyright>Joseph Lennox</Copyright>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/jlennox/NvEncSharp/</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/jlennox/NvEncSharp/</RepositoryUrl>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="System.Memory" Version="4.5.3" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\NvEncSharp.Cuda.Library\NvEncSharp.Cuda.Library.vcxproj" PrivateAssets="All" Condition="'$(BuildCudaLibrary)' == 'true'" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\readme.md">
      <Pack>true</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
    <Content Include="lib\runtimes\win-x64\native\**\*.dll">
      <PackagePath>runtimes/win-x64/native</PackagePath>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Pack>true</Pack>
    </Content>
    <Content Include="lib\Lennox.NvEncSharp.targets">
      <PackagePath>lib/netstandard2.0;lib/net461;build/net461;lib/netcoreapp2.0;build</PackagePath>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Pack>true</Pack>
    </Content>
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
